IS BEUFORD BARGAIN BOTTOM
- 下一个
伯福德讨价还价已经触底

17:47.758 --> 17:50.931
IN CONVENIENCE STORE CAPER.
在便利店里胡闹。

17:50.931 --> 17:54.206
beep! beep! beep!
嘟！嘟！嘟！

17:54.206 --> 17:56.758
- UH, YOU CHARGED ME
THREE TIMES.
- 呃，你向我收费
三次。

17:56.758 --> 17:59.310
- YEAH,
THREE TIMES THE FLAVOR,
- 是的，
三倍的味道，

17:59.310 --> 18:01.413
THREE TIMES THE PRICE.
三倍的价格。

18:01.413 --> 18:03.862
[cheers and applause]
[欢呼和掌声]

18:03.862 --> 18:08.724
- AND DWIGHT T. WAD
IN TYING UP LOOSE ENDS.
- 和德怀特·T·沃德
收拾残局。

18:15.517 --> 18:17.034
[cheers and applause]
[欢呼和掌声]

18:17.034 --> 18:19.241
- AW, JEEZ.
- 噢，天啊。

18:19.241 --> 18:21.965
I DIDN'’T THINK THE COMPETITION
WOULD BE SO STIFF THIS YEAR.
我没想到比赛
今年会如此僵硬。

18:21.965 --> 18:24.586
I'’M GONNA NEED YOUR HELP
ON THIS ONE.
我需要你的帮助
关于这一点。

18:24.586 --> 18:28.172
[whispering]
[耳语]

18:28.172 --> 18:31.827
- WELL, THAT'’S HIGHLY
UNCONVENTIONAL, BUT OKAY.
- 嗯，非常好
非常规，但是还可以。

18:31.827 --> 18:33.758
WE WILL NOW HEAR A TESTIMONY
我们现在将听到证词

18:33.758 --> 18:37.275
FROM A KRUSTY KRAB EMPLOYEE.
来自 Krusty Krab 员工。

18:37.275 --> 18:39.586
- I NEED YOU TO TESTIFY
ABOUT HOW CHEAP I AM,
- 我需要你作证
关于我有多廉价，

18:39.586 --> 18:42.172
SO IF YOU NEED TO DO
A LITTLE EXAGGERATING...
所以如果你需要这样做
有点夸张...

18:51.000 --> 18:52.137
YOU'’RE NOT GETTING IT,
ARE YOU?
你不明白，
你是吗？

18:52.137 --> 18:53.965
- MM-MM.
- MM-MM。
- MM-MM。
- MM-MM。
- MM-MM。
- MM-MM。
- MM-MM。
- MM-MM。

18:53.965 --> 18:56.034
- EXAGGERATING
IS LIKE TELLING THE TRUTH,
- 夸张
就像说实话一样，

18:56.034 --> 18:58.448
ONLY WITH LITTLE LIES
SPRINKLED IN
只有小谎言
洒入

18:58.448 --> 19:02.103
TO MAKE IT TRUE...ER.
让它成为现实......呃。

19:02.103 --> 19:04.344
- YOU'’RE TEACHING ME TO LIE?
- 你在教我撒谎？

19:04.344 --> 19:06.206
LYING IS WRONG, MR. KRABS.
说谎是错误的，先生。螃蟹。

19:06.206 --> 19:08.137
- NO, NO, NO, NO, NO, NO.
- 不，不，不，不，不，不。

19:08.137 --> 19:10.517
EXAGGERATING IS COMPLETELY
DIFFERENT FROM LYING.
完全是夸大其辞
与说谎不同。

19:10.517 --> 19:12.310
YOU'’RE TAKING THE TRUTH
你说的是实话

19:12.310 --> 19:16.655
AND JUST SEASONING IT
WITH LITTLE LIES.
只是调味
很少撒谎。

19:16.655 --> 19:19.172
I MEAN, JUST BECAUSE
YOU PUT SALT ON A KRABBY PATTY,
我的意思是，只是因为
你把盐放在蟹肉饼上，

19:19.172 --> 19:22.896
IT DOESN'’T MAKE IT
A "SALTY PATTY," DOES IT?
它没有成功
是“咸肉饼”吗？

19:22.896 --> 19:24.068
- NO?
- 不？

19:24.068 --> 19:25.827
- WELL, GOOD ENOUGH.
- 好吧，够了。

19:25.827 --> 19:26.931
JUST MAKE SURE
YOU EXAGGERATE ENOUGH
请确保
你太夸张了

19:26.931 --> 19:27.517
FOR ME TO WIN.
让我赢。

19:30.620 --> 19:31.931
[microphone feedback squeals]
[麦克风反馈尖叫声]

19:33.827 --> 19:39.620
- UM, MR. KRABS
HAS ALWAYS BEEN VERY--
- 嗯，先生。蟹蟹
一直都是非常--

19:39.620 --> 19:42.241
THE VERY--
非常——

19:42.241 --> 19:44.586
VERY RED.
非常红。

19:44.586 --> 19:45.689
smack!
咂！

19:45.689 --> 19:47.172
- EXAGGERATE!
- 夸张了！

19:47.172 --> 19:48.655
- OH...
BLUE!
- 哦...
蓝色！

19:48.655 --> 19:51.103
- NO, ABOUT ME BEING CHEAP.
- 不，是因为我便宜。

19:51.103 --> 19:55.103
- UM, MR. KRABS IS--IS--
IS A VERY GENEROUS EMPLOYER.
- 嗯，先生。螃蟹是——是——
是一个非常慷慨的雇主。

19:55.103 --> 19:57.000
[all gasp]
[全都喘气]

19:57.000 --> 19:59.517
- NO, NO, NO, NO,
EXAGGERATE THE OTHER WAY!
- 不，不，不，不，
用另一种方式夸大其词！

19:59.517 --> 20:01.137
- DE-EXAGGERATE, UM...
- 去夸张，嗯……

20:01.137 --> 20:03.172
HE'’S NOT DOING IT FOR THE MONEY.
他这样做不是为了钱。

20:03.172 --> 20:06.896
HE IS DOING IT
FOR HIS LOYAL EMPLOYEES.
他正在做这件事
为了他忠诚的员工。

20:06.896 --> 20:08.862
